cctv-viewer (2.2.7-1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Added intuitive viewport right-click menu options ("Stopklatka" and "Odtwarzaj") for rapid viewport snapshot and archive playback operations.
  * Implemented interactive volume slider HUD and quick-mute/maximize buttons directly on camera viewports with a fullscreen focus safeguard.
  * Overhauled PCM audio handling pipeline: integrated direct streaming to QAudioOutput with a robust 5-frame sample rate estimation debounce rule to prevent rapid recreation thrashing and UI thread deadlocks under ALSA/PulseAudio/Pipewire.
  * Added a minimum 2-second cooldown on audio output recreations, robust validation against corrupted sample rate/channel parameters, and a 64KB buffer to mitigate network jitter and audio dropouts.
  * Implemented automated, immediate live view grid muting upon opening the Archive/Playback window, eliminating sound overlapping.
  * Introduced standard SnapshotSavedDialog central notifications with custom dark-gray and celadon-bordered styling, a 10-second auto-close timer, and a high-contrast 'Przeglądaj' (Browse) button to open the folder externally in the system's default file manager.
  * Enriched the Help/Instructions window with a detailed 'Opis działania przycisków' (Description of button operations) chapter containing native Base64 vector SVG icons. The Help window is now configured to automatically launch centered on first-time startup.
  * Changed the default startup behavior to display the floating top toolbar, which can be customized via the new setting 'Domyślnie pokazuj pasek górny po otwarciu okna'.
  * Resolved application crash at startup on Debian/Ubuntu and other multi-arch derivative distributions by using a dynamic INSTALL_RPATH pointing to CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR/kvision (by moving GNUInstallDirs early), making manual ldconfig hacks obsolete.

